From c1b398c391ea74b3b0984d58221d20900e9708a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy <andylee77@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:44:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] raptor agent: config reads without a process per field;
 detection settings

The agent adapter and agent-lib as the port's development tree runs them. On
top of the adapter of the Thingino series:

- GET /config, the stream blocks and the image block are printed through
  helpers that hand their result back in a variable, from sections read once
  and an ISP state parsed once, so a field no longer costs a copy of the shell
  (and often a tr or an awk). agent-lib quotes a string that has nothing to
  escape without awk.
- Detection, for rvd's IVS: settings/motion/algorithm, model, num-classes,
  conf-threshold and nms-threshold, beside the sensitivity and cooldown
  settings the agent already had; rvd reads them at its start, so each
  answers that a stream restart applies it. settings/motion/draw-boxes
  switches the boxes rod burns into the sub stream, at once;
  settings/motion/labels gives the class names (a <model>.txt beside the
  model, else the public models' names). The capabilities list the
  algorithms whose libraries the image has and the model files; the runtime
  read "detections" gives rvd's current boxes with the sub stream's size.
- Turning detection on answers restart_required when rvd runs no IVS
  channel (it builds one only at its start), so the page offers the video
  restart instead of saying "saved" while nothing detects.
- The model list also offers the models folder of an SD card
  (/mnt/mmcblk*/models/), so a model can be tried without a new image, and
  .mgk models beside .bin ones. The model method is offered when the image
  has the JZDL engine or Ingenic's Uranus runtime for the T41's NNA
  (liburanus_core.so); the .mgk models need the NNA backend proposed as
  gtxaspec/raptor-hal#21.
- settings/motion/detect-interval-ms sets [motion] detect_interval_ms, the
  least time between two inferences and with it detection's CPU cost; rvd
  reads it once gtxaspec/raptor#96 is in, and ignores it before.

Generic: none of it depends on the SigmaStar platform. On the host the
adapter's answers match ones saved from two Infinity6C cameras, which have
no IVS, and its detection answers pass a test against a stand-in raptorctl.
